{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For</b> — the meaning is: you cut down the trees of Lebanon for your building." "<b>and the violence of beasts</b> — and your violence: you used to terrify the beasts, and behold He will terrify them [sc. you] — like יקימן ישיבן, many [as] females." "<b>the blood of men</b> — and behold, over all, his evil passed."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The Hebrew of the final phrase is compressed and its syntax uncertain; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:00.581981633Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}